Blockchain technology offers a promising solution for enhancing data security and privacy in Vehicle Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs), which serve as a critical component of Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS). This paper provides a comprehensive survey of Blockchain applications in VANETs, covering foundational concepts, key challenges, and recent advancements. We examine the integration of Blockchain with VANETs, outline their core characteristics, and categorize existing Blockchain-based VANET architectures. Furthermore, we analyze various security protocols designed to address specific VANET challenges, discuss potential risks associated with Blockchain in VANETs, and propose future research directions. The survey concludes with an overview of relevant open-source Blockchain-based VANET systems. Ultimately, this work aims to guide researchers in developing effective security protocols for VANETs through the adoption of Blockchain technology.

